<title>INDIA: India April exports down 10 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>India April exports down 10 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The value of India's merchandise exports fell about 10 percent in April compared with the same month in 1996, a government official said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Last June, the Commerce Ministry reported that exports were valued at $2.81 billion in April 1996. The figure was subject to revision.</p>
<p>The ministry was expected to release merchandise trade data for April later on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
